/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  membrane18_nf_feed_and_bleed / system/solverDict

  ONE recycle, so ONE tear.  `Recycle` is the back edge: it is produced by
  the splitter (declared LAST) and consumed by the mixer (declared FIRST), so
  the sequential plan cannot reach it without a cut, and the engine refuses
  by name if the cut is not declared.  Its seed lives in 0/Recycle like every
  other stream's state -- the author's, and announced as such.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

tearStreams           ( Recycle );
recycleSolver          Newton;

//  THE TEAR IS CONVERGED TO 1e-10, NOT TO THE DEFAULT (C390 sweep fix).  The plant's first law
//  compares the streams of the last sweep with the tear the mixer was handed; at the default tolerance
//  that difference was 3.8e-7 of the enthalpy flow, which the report read as 0.042 kW of unexplained
//  energy against an exchanged scale of 0.57 kW (the module's isothermal duty, Q_kW).  Newton on the
//  tear needs three iterations either way; the residual is now 0.0000 kW.
recycleTol 1e-10;
